<title>BRAZIL: MOTORCYCLING-PRACTICE TIMES FOR BRAZILIAN GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTORCYCLING-PRACTICE TIMES FOR BRAZILIAN GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading 500cc motorcycle practice times in the first official qualifying session on Friday for the Brazilian Grand Prix on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Michael Doohan (Australia), Honda, one minute 54.758 seconds</p>
<p>2. Norifumi Abe (Japan), Yamaha, 1:54.968</p>
<p>3. Jean Michel Bayle (France), Yamaha, 1:55.056</p>
<p>4. Alex Criville (Spain), Honda, 1:55.167</p>
<p>5. Alexandre Barros (Brazil), Honda, 1:55.552</p>
<p>6. Carlos Checa (Spain), Honda), 1:55.818</p>
<p>7. Luca Cadalora (Italy), Honda, 1:55.868</p>
<p>8. Kenny Roberts jnr (U.S.), Yamaha, 1:55.876</p>
<p>9. Tadayuki Okada (Japan), Honda, 1:56.158</p>
<p>10. Loris Capirossi (Italy), Yamaha, 1:56.505</p>
</text>
